Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.33 log what the Items menu allows on Cross for equipment

Owner report (preview.47): "selecting a weapon in the Items menu does nothing; it
only works from Status > Equipment". Read from the decomp, this is the original
behavior: STSTATUS_runItemList only acts on Cross for the first list (option
0) and there only for an item with ITEM_USE_MENU; weapons, armor and
accessories are listed and described, never used (no sound either), and patch
0128 touches only equip_panel.c. This patch changes no behavior: it logs one
`dw3-items-menu: Cross on weapon N (list L): the original game does nothing
here ...` line per press, so an OLED log says what the game allows. Policy and
log text in port/items_menu/items_menu.c.

--- a2/src/menus/field_menu/item_list.c
+++ b2/src/menus/field_menu/item_list.c
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
    panels (STSTATUS_createItemList): its rodata starts at 0x80082B90 (USA). */
 
 #include "menus/field_menu.h"
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_items_menu.h"
+#endif
 
 /* Creates the item list's windows: its title, two columns of 8 items, the page
    number, the page arrows and the cursor */
@@ -207,7 +210,28 @@
                         STSTATUS_showItemHelp(panel->screen, -1);
                         panel->substate++;
                     }
+#if PORT_HOST
+                    else {
+                        /* the original game does nothing here, silently */
+                        dw3_port_items_menu_selected(panel->list, panel->screen->item, 0,
+                                                     ITEM_FUNCS.isKind(panel->screen->item, ITEM_KIND_WEAPON) ? ITEM_KIND_WEAPON :
+                                                     ITEM_FUNCS.isKind(panel->screen->item, ITEM_KIND_ARMOR) ? ITEM_KIND_ARMOR :
+                                                     ITEM_FUNCS.isKind(panel->screen->item, ITEM_KIND_ACCESSORY) ? ITEM_KIND_ACCESSORY : 0);
+                    }
+#endif
+                }
+#if PORT_HOST
+                else if (panel->cursor >= 0 && panel->cursor < panel->count) {
+                    /* the other lists (weapons, armor, accessories, ...) only list and
+                       describe: the original game does nothing on Cross, silently */
+                    s32 item = panel->items[panel->cursor];
+
+                    dw3_port_items_menu_selected(panel->list, item, 1,
+                                                 ITEM_FUNCS.isKind(item, ITEM_KIND_WEAPON) ? ITEM_KIND_WEAPON :
+                                                 ITEM_FUNCS.isKind(item, ITEM_KIND_ARMOR) ? ITEM_KIND_ARMOR :
+                                                 ITEM_FUNCS.isKind(item, ITEM_KIND_ACCESSORY) ? ITEM_KIND_ACCESSORY : 0);
                 }
+#endif
             } else if (PAD_PRESSED(PAD_TRIANGLE)) {
                 SOUND.playSound(SOUND_MENU_CANCEL);
                 panel->screen->itemIndex = -1;
